@reporter there is none, also had to be dropped for 27.1

Research state is: that i.e. `in:files` is supported i.e. to limit it to just search in files but currently there is no other limiting/filtering criteria present for unified search to limit it's search scope for files. so anything we want would need to be build (hence v28).

Si for example for files the statement is that anything we can do in dav search should be relatively easy to be added to search (for files)

@participant2 this is now in for 28, so we can proceed. :) The direction with the mockup is great, only can you combine both the mockups made, so basically to the latest one add the following:
- [x] "Places" dropdown should be converted to show at least the first few apps as chips, then a 3-dot menu, otherwise it is not as discoverable
- [x] The top mockup has the additional buttons like "Search in Talk", "Search in Contacts", these would be good to add back as a jumping off point to the in-app-searches. The "Load more results" should continue to behave like now as loading the next few results in place.

@reporter On second thought the multi-select cannot be an action menu, just have a look at the amount of places that we have in the global search. The multi-select allows quick search, adding and removing of these. An action menu would complicate things a lot.

@participant9 shouldn't we use all those data sets for their respective categories? For example, if a search yields results both from calendar and files, I think should be able to filter "person" in both datasets. 

> Do we limit time ranges to the timezone of the searching user

I would do this yes.

@participant9 It should probably be a merge of the datasets you mentioned above. But I don't know exactly how to answer this question as that would be a bit counterintuitive (duplicates, triplicates, etc.). 
Early on I encountered several possible conflicts that will arise from using a fixed set of filters with so many different search providers. And many more that I haven't thought about could pop up since any app can register a provider. That's why in the original proposal I argued for a simpler solution for global search and more complex filtering only in-app ([here](https://github.com/nextcloud/server/issues/39162#issuecomment-1631801315) and [here](https://github.com/nextcloud/server/issues/39162#issuecomment-1635223315)).
@reporter what would you do here? Could we go back to a simpler version for this?
